        </p>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>1. What is Cyber Security?</h2>

            <p>
                Cyber Security is the practice of protecting
                computers, networks, applications and data
                from unauthorized access and attacks.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>2. Authentication</h2>

            <p>
                Authentication is the process of verifying
                the identity of a user before allowing access
                to a system.
            </p>

            <p>
                Example: Username and Password.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>3. Encryption</h2>

            <p>
                Encryption converts readable data into an
                unreadable form to protect information.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>4. Firewall</h2>

            <p>
                A firewall monitors and controls network traffic
                based on security rules.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="topic">
            <h2>5. Common Cyber Attacks</h2>

            <p>
                Some common attacks include phishing,
                malware, password attacks and denial-of-service attacks.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>

